A||||25||baggy||TOM'S SCOOPS||||1||
Z||000000||baggy||01-25-2000||09:55 PM||||can anybody tell me how the rear deck scoop would help airflow across the motor..<BR>to be totaly honest..<BR>it looks like the heat comin' off of my Iron Duke would melt it..<BR>I gotta enough melted stuff on the back of my firewall..LOL||||reg||1
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||01-25-2000||11:12 PM||||I beleive the principal behind it is that since heat rises giving it a place to go would be ideal. As your Fiero is moving the moving air would draw out the heat that has risen to the top of engine through the scoop. Regularly this heat is swept downward and out the bottom rear of the car. It is a sound idea.<P>Also if your iron duke is melting things you might want to replace your O2 sensor. The engine might be running rich.<P>I do not work for or even know Tom personally (Though 88 Fiero says hes a good guy) and have not actually bought anything from Tom (yet) so you can consider this an unbiased (though I would like to see him in our club) opinion about the rear deck scoop.<P>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 01-25-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 01-25-2000).]||||reg||3
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||01-25-2000||11:25 PM||||Baggy I have Tom's rear deck lid scoop and WKDFIRO is right it does the same as the rear deck grills. And it also looks darn good!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||WKDFIRO||01-25-2000||11:46 PM||||I like the way it buffs out that "power hump" without, as Tom says, being gaudy.||||reg||14
Z||000004||TOM||01-26-2000||10:14 AM||||And to add to that. The fiero as are most cars. The shape is similar to an airplane wing. This causes lift. There for the air is trying to go up. The engine compartment is designed to help that with the vents on top. Most cars forct the air up over the engine then back down. This just help give the air another place to go. It would probably wvwn work with solid vents from an 84. The undersid can be covered with a reflective heat barrier if you are worried about it. But if it is not melting the decklid then the scoop will be fine. It is a high quality than the decklid||||reg||1
Z||000005||Gokart||01-26-2000||09:21 PM||||I can't wait till spring so I can put mine on! Got it primed and smooth as a baby's bottom! MAN, I WISH I HAD A GARAGE!||||reg||14
Z||000006||MCordray||01-26-2000||09:48 PM||||What rear scoop are we talking about? Is this like the Indy over-the-roof scoop? Does Tom make these?||||reg||5
Z||000007||TOM||01-26-2000||09:53 PM||||I have one of those that I havent had time to make molds from. The scoop in question is a low extractor scoop||||reg||1
Z||000008||william_thorniii||01-26-2000||09:54 PM||||Mark,<P>Yes Tom makes a scoop... I have forgotten his address.  It is similar to a scoop that you have seen on many muscle cars only in the back with the opening to the rear.  It has a wide and low profile unlike most of the Mustang scoops that everyone else puts on there.  Since it is so wide, it covers the entire hump that is present on the later years Fiero decklids.<P>Sidenote... sorry that I didn't contact you the other week.  I will be in Cincy again at the end of next week.  I would like to come by and check out your x-tra lid if possible.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||4
