Z||000013||dogtired||01-27-2000||02:14 PM||||Tom<BR>I like the scoop! Read your ad on your page & is says bolt on?? Would you please elaborate on the installation??? <BR>Will it fit all Fiero Deck lids???  84?? Notchback??  Fastback??<BR>Would a car with a wing hide it too much??<BR>Just some thoughts? Maybe Someday?  THANKS||||reg||6
Z||000014||DaRkLoRD||01-27-2000||08:22 PM||||Tom's scoop (which looks awesome BTW) fits all decklids.. mounting it without cutting a hole in the decklid is pointless. it wouldn't serve any purpose, whereas if you cut the decklid and then install the scoop, it's functional.<P>Go to the Mods section of the Fiero Project ( <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A> ) and click on the Exterior Mods section. DXR_DAD has a decklid scoop installed on his 86 SE, and it looks great. There's an article written by him about the project, well worth reading if you're interested in this modification.<P>I'll post a photo of the installed scoop.||||reg||1
Z||000015||DaRkLoRD||01-27-2000||08:27 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/00000003.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||MCordray||01-27-2000||09:11 PM||||Tom,<P>Nice looking scoop! I'm torn between your scoop & the over-the-roof. If you were to make an over-the-roof, what price range would you be looking at? Would it fit Fastback GT's?<P>William T.,<P>Let me know when you're in Cincy again & I'll show you the decklid.||||reg||14
